<title>ITALY: Forli airport says 1996 airfreight down slightly.</title>
<headline>Forli airport says 1996 airfreight down slightly.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scheduled air cargo traffic at Forli airport fell to 2,090 tonnes in 1996 from 2,133 the previous year, Forli airport authority.</p>
<p>It added that the top export destination was Algeria with poultry, chicks and food products the main export cargo.</p>
<p>Airfreight imports were dominated by winter fruit and vegetables grown in Ethiopia by Italian farmers from the Romagna region.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel:44-171-542-7706 Fax+ 5017.</p>
</text>
